#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054425 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054848 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "33551349-bb39-5a79-bf56-a4df753201ed" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Elements of a Set"}] :question/id #uuid "16e0f524-49b5-549d-8e60-8597379c4350" :question/math-academy-id "e-13134" :question/problem "List the elements of the following set: \n\n$$\nA = \\big\\{a, c,3, \\{c,3 \\}, \\emptyset, \\{\\emptyset\\}\\big\\}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The elements of the set $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\na, \\quad c, \\quad 3, \\quad \\{c,3\\}, \\quad \\emptyset, \\quad \\{\\emptyset\\}\n$$\n\n**Watch Out!**\n\n- The elements $c,3,$ and $\\{c,3\\}$ are three separate entities. The first two are the elements $c$ and $3,$ and the third is a set *containing* these two elements.\n\n- The elements $\\emptyset$ and $\\{ \\emptyset \\}$ are also separate entities. The first one is the empty set (i.e., the set containing no elements), while the second is a set that contains the empty set."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054426 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054849 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "de59db4d-82d5-5bad-a559-bf5396375355" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Non-Sets"}] :question/id #uuid "046f7284-3715-555c-bdc9-c108db061205" :question/math-academy-id "e-13135" :question/problem "Which of the following is **not** a set?\n\nI. $\\{ 2, 4, 6 \\}$\n\nII. $\\{ \\{ 2 \\}, \\{ 4, 6 \\} \\}$\n\nIII. $2, 4, 6$\n\nIV. $\\emptyset$" :question/worked-solution "A set is a collection of elements listed between two braces (curly brackets). However, note that the null set (the set that does not contain any elements) can be written as either $\\{\\}$ or $\\emptyset.$\n\n- $\\{ 2, 4, 6 \\}$ is a set. The elements are $2,$ $4,$ and $6,$ and they are listed between two braces.\n\n- $\\{ \\{ 2 \\}, \\{ 4, 6 \\} \\}$ is a set. The elements are $\\{ 2 \\}$ and $\\{ 4, 6 \\},$ and are listed between the two outermost braces.\n\n- $2, 4, 6$ is *not* a set. The numbers $2,$ $4,$ and $6$ are *not* listed between two braces.\n\n- $\\emptyset$ is the empty set. Therefore, it is a set.\n\nIn conclusion, only III is not a set."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054427 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054850 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "900f0d3d-6a5c-53b2-b987-eee1a8963b6b" :knowledge-point/title "Using Element Notation"}] :question/id #uuid "5404d545-570b-53d7-b16a-b23a371d4abd" :question/math-academy-id "e-13136" :question/problem "Write the following statement using element notation:\n\n$\\qquad$ $1$ and $2$ are elements of a set $S,$ but $3,$ $4,$ and $5$ are not." :question/worked-solution "If $a$ is an element of $S,$ we write $a \\in S.$ Otherwise, if $a$ is *not* an element of $S,$ we write $a \\notin S.$\n\n- Since $1$ and $2$ are elements of $S,$ we write $1,2 \\in S.$\n\n- Since $3,$ $4,$ and $5$ are *not* elements of $S,$ we write $3,4,5 \\notin S.$\n\nAll together, we have the following statement:\n\n$$\n1,2 \\in S\\quad \\textrm{and}\\quad 3,4,5 \\notin S\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054428 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054851 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ceb6c84-a16b-5519-abd6-d2bb72ea81d3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Set Corresponding to a Description"}] :question/id #uuid "0684e366-bcf4-5b08-8eae-6600a88e2920" :question/math-academy-id "e-13137" :question/problem "Express the following sets using an ellipsis:\n\n- The set $X$ of all positive integers greater than or equal to $10$\n\n- The set $Y$ of integers less than zero\n\n- The set $A$ of all natural numbers greater than $5$ and less than $5\\, 005$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that an ellipsis means \"and so on up to\" if it's followed by a specific element, or \"and so on\" if not.\n\n- To express the set $X,$ we start with the first positive integer greater than or equal to $10,$ which is $10.$ The next integer is $11,$ the one after that is $12,$ and so on, which we denote with an ellipsis:\n\n$$\nX = \\{10, 11, 12, \\ldots \\}\n$$\n\n- To express the set $Y,$ we start with the first integer less than zero, which is $-1.$ The next integer less than zero is $-2,$ the one after that is $-3,$ and so on, which we denote with an ellipsis:\n\n$$\nY = \\{ -1, -2, -3, \\ldots \\}\n$$\n\nHowever, note that it is conventional to write a set of numbers from least to greatest, just like is shown on the number line. Writing the elements of $Y$ from least to greatest, we have\n\n$$\nY = \\{ \\ldots , -3, -2, -1\\}.\n$$\n\n- To express the set $A,$ we start with the first positive integer greater than $5,$ which is $6.$ The next integer is $7,$ the one after that is $8,$ and so on up to $5\\, 004$ (the largest integer less than $5\\, 005$). So, we have\n\n$$\nA = \\{6, 7, 8, \\ldots , 5004\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514420 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054850 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "900f0d3d-6a5c-53b2-b987-eee1a8963b6b" :knowledge-point/title "Using Element Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0be63167-6f24-5aa9-82e2-881c75a4fcf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "v,w\\in B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513560} {:answer/id #uuid "11399e5f-3461-57e4-bb07-738143f0cb77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x,y,z\\notin B$ and $v,w\\in B$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513576} {:answer/id #uuid "1c2bc8fd-0245-51f5-9eb9-80380f45f77c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x,y,z\\in B$ and $v,w\\notin B$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513606} {:answer/id #uuid "5be50ca2-0ec1-5976-816f-395c808ddc72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x,y,z\\notin B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513778} {:answer/id #uuid "dc2f42fb-f6fb-5af0-bf6c-4e468f6a011c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x,y\\in B$ and $z,v,w\\notin B$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514109}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c2bc8fd-0245-51f5-9eb9-80380f45f77c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x,y,z\\in B$ and $v,w\\notin B$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513606} :answer-field/id #uuid "83ddee6b-0ee6-53e7-9738-f66e538f4e76" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514289}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6b96bbb9-30d0-511e-a26c-5b394ffc1b3c" :question/math-academy-id "q-101922" :question/problem "If $x,y,$ and $z$ are elements of $B$, but $v$ and $w$ are not, then which of the following is true?" :question/worked-solution "If $a$ is an element of $S,$ we write $a\\in S.$ Otherwise, if $a$ is *not* an element of $S,$ we write $a\\notin S.$\n\n- Since $x,y,$ and $z$ are elements of $B,$ we write $x,y,z\\in B.$\n\n- Since $v$ and $w$ are *not* elements of $B,$ we write $v,w\\notin B.$\n\nAll together, we have the following statement:\n\n$\\,$  $x,y,z\\in B$ and $v,w\\notin B$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514419 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054850 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "900f0d3d-6a5c-53b2-b987-eee1a8963b6b" :knowledge-point/title "Using Element Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0447a795-c6d5-5dfd-ada1-ec30242c71e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${3}^{4}\\in B$ and ${2}^{5},{2}^{7}\\notin B$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513541} {:answer/id #uuid "430f142b-079d-5d36-b9ed-c7fcb1a257fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{3}^{4},{5}^{0}\\in B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513710} {:answer/id #uuid "64079805-e640-5e9e-b17b-eef19f4b9ee0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${2}^{5},{2}^{7},{2}^{9}\\in B$ and ${3}^{4},{5}^{0}\\notin B$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513801} {:answer/id #uuid "6e9a1d45-8d06-5fa1-807a-558577aa972d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${3}^{4},{5}^{0}\\in B$ and ${2}^{5},{2}^{7},{2}^{9}\\notin B$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513830} {:answer/id #uuid "83e1229a-7aa6-5f6e-abda-ca318568130c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2}^{5},{2}^{7},{2}^{9}\\notin B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513876}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "64079805-e640-5e9e-b17b-eef19f4b9ee0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${2}^{5},{2}^{7},{2}^{9}\\in B$ and ${3}^{4},{5}^{0}\\notin B$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513801} :answer-field/id #uuid "666a3742-fc17-5528-9ff4-7003969fc507" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514276}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6ae10c4a-b478-5b9e-9599-7eb7b75dca9d" :question/math-academy-id "q-101933" :question/problem "If ${2}^{5},{2}^{7},$ and ${2}^{9}$ are elements of $B$, but ${3}^{4}$ and ${5}^{0}$ are not, then which of the following is true?" :question/worked-solution "If $a$ is an element of $S,$ we write $a\\in S.$ Otherwise, if $a$ is *not* an element of $S,$ we write $a\\notin S.$\n\n- Since ${2}^{5},{2}^{7},$ and ${2}^{9}$ are elements of $B,$ we write ${2}^{5},{2}^{7},{2}^{9}\\in B.$\n\n- Since ${3}^{4}$ and ${5}^{0}$ are *not* elements of $B,$ we write ${3}^{4},{5}^{0}\\notin B.$\n\nAll together, we have the following statement:\n\n$\\,$  ${2}^{5},{2}^{7},{2}^{9}\\in B$ and ${3}^{4},{5}^{0}\\notin B$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514414 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054849 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "de59db4d-82d5-5bad-a559-bf5396375355" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Non-Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b6319c4-4efb-5c74-bead-1ca09a8e128b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513686} {:answer/id #uuid "650db520-6fe2-5a0f-a847-f67969871c86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∅" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513803} {:answer/id #uuid "6e636f0b-5913-5738-8061-83223afb839d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\{\\}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513829} {:answer/id #uuid "847ea62c-8079-5329-b9a6-20b01100c875" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{7},\\frac{2}{5},\\frac{2}{3},\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513877} {:answer/id #uuid "a6ae7272-dfb4-51e4-813a-3b640ded878e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\frac{2}{7},\\frac{2}{5},\\frac{2}{3},\\frac{1}{2}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513961}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "847ea62c-8079-5329-b9a6-20b01100c875" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{7},\\frac{2}{5},\\frac{2}{3},\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513877} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4989f7b-3998-56d8-84b3-b2b2b96bef9c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514319}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "68a9ef69-1a68-5a42-bd02-0ed93671db30" :question/math-academy-id "q-104392" :question/problem "Which of the following is **not** a set?" :question/worked-solution "A set is a collection of elements listed between two braces (curly brackets). However, note that the null set (the set that does not contain any elements) can be written as either $\\{\\}$ or $∅.$\n\n- $\\frac{2}{7},\\frac{2}{5},\\frac{2}{3},\\frac{1}{2}$ is *not* a set. The numbers $\\frac{2}{7},$ $\\frac{2}{5},$ $\\frac{2}{3},$ and $\\frac{1}{2}$ are *not* listed between two braces.\n\nAll the other choices are sets.\n\n- $\\{\\frac{2}{7},\\frac{2}{5},\\frac{2}{3},\\frac{1}{2}\\}$ is a set. The elements are $\\frac{2}{7},\\frac{2}{5},\\frac{2}{3},\\frac{1}{2}$ and they are listed between two braces.\n\n- $\\{\\{\\}\\}$ is a set. It contains a single element, $\\{\\},$ and this element is between two braces.\n\n- $\\{\\}$ is a set. It is the null set.\n\n- $∅$ is a set. It is the null set."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514425 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054851 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ceb6c84-a16b-5519-abd6-d2bb72ea81d3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Set Corresponding to a Description"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ae35147-d8d9-5552-8ef0-e5921f034714" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{-20,-10,0,10\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513602} {:answer/id #uuid "1f52347f-2916-55e5-abc8-4a087e3c5c15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{-20,-15,-10,…,5\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513614} {:answer/id #uuid "2fcc56eb-0a58-5a35-8189-ba6da205b93b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{-20,-15,-10,…,10\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513659} {:answer/id #uuid "ae3c24a5-7306-5650-af15-bc07972ae031" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{-25,-20,-15,…,10\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513989} {:answer/id #uuid "b9858cce-17aa-5336-a354-b3bcd71e3c17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{-20,-15,-10,…,15\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514023}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2fcc56eb-0a58-5a35-8189-ba6da205b93b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{-20,-15,-10,…,10\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513659} :answer-field/id #uuid "6bf3c0e7-4219-5e25-bc7d-63783b1bd456" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514279}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "76066cd5-d606-50ce-8894-909f30c9f6a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-104952" :question/problem "Which set represents all integers divisible by $5$ from $-21$ to $11?$" :question/worked-solution "To express the desired set, we start with the first integer divisible by $5$ greater than or equal to $-21,$ which is $-20.$ The next integer divisible by $5$ is $-15,$ the one after that is $-10,$ and so on up to $10$ (which is the last number that is divisible by $5$ and less than or equal to $11$).\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\{-20,-15,-10,…,10\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054970 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054848 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "33551349-bb39-5a79-bf56-a4df753201ed" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Elements of a Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34d077d0-b217-5819-942e-7a3ca19d31ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051353} {:answer/id #uuid "605ca6b6-a3df-57e6-808c-7dd385c9eb3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051354} {:answer/id #uuid "6d231f10-902f-5c12-93a2-d50e881243f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051355} {:answer/id #uuid "5e87d1b9-c21c-5e07-8bcb-e7801cafe650" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{e\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513786} {:answer/id #uuid "dbed2e9b-2062-58e1-bbcb-34bffd5958e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{d\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514107}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e87d1b9-c21c-5e07-8bcb-e7801cafe650" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{e\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513786} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8aa0f78-c767-5f71-9f45-b378b603712a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051350}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a7b3410f-37c1-59bb-9c9d-28bb9b75dbb5" :question/math-academy-id "q-1150" :question/problem "Which of the following is an element of the set $C=\\{\\{a\\},\\,b,\\,\\{c\\},\\,d,\\,\\{e\\}\\}?$" :question/worked-solution "The elements of our set are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{a\\},\\,b,\\,\\{c\\},\\,d,\\,\\{e\\}\n$$\n\nAmong the given options, the only element that belongs to the set is $\\{e\\}.$\n\n**Watch out!** Note that $e$ is *not* an element of our set. Our set contains an element $\\{e\\}$ that is a set itself."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054972 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054850 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "900f0d3d-6a5c-53b2-b987-eee1a8963b6b" :knowledge-point/title "Using Element Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c63e39c-ecfa-5d5a-9f4f-bd3b390019cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "d,e\\in S" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513687} {:answer/id #uuid "5b38006e-2ad1-52eb-ad48-c5a73b96e9b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a,b,c\\in S$ and $d,e\\notin S$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513775} {:answer/id #uuid "b8b84e9a-76dd-5810-b594-e0762d48398c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a,b,c\\notin S" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514022} {:answer/id #uuid "de04cc81-7aaa-50c1-a197-5a3b9ca7cbe4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a,b,c\\notin S$ and $d,e\\in S$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514114} {:answer/id #uuid "e95b841b-9de7-591f-9b54-0662ea51e111" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a,b\\in S$ and $c,d,e\\notin S$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514142}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b38006e-2ad1-52eb-ad48-c5a73b96e9b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a,b,c\\in S$ and $d,e\\notin S$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513775} :answer-field/id #uuid "bbeb8dbc-dca5-5d86-981e-fbd5f85769d7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051362}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "126eb637-e5ca-5143-b535-559e40bc4ac8" :question/math-academy-id "q-1166" :question/problem "If $a,b,$ and $c$ are elements of $S$, but $d$ and $e$ are not, then which of the following is true?" :question/worked-solution "If $a$ is an element of $S,$ we write $a\\in S.$ Otherwise, if $a$ is *not* an element of $S,$ we write $a\\notin S.$\n\n- Since $a,b,$ and $c$ are elements of $S,$ we write $a,b,c\\in S.$\n\n- Since $d$ and $e$ are *not* elements of $S,$ we write $d,e\\notin S.$\n\nAll together, we have the following statement:\n\n$\\,$  $a,b,c\\in S$ and $d,e\\notin S$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514460 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054848 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "33551349-bb39-5a79-bf56-a4df753201ed" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Elements of a Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24a04d7d-0766-53f9-bf1a-56af16878e80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "◻" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513634} {:answer/id #uuid "6e44578a-0359-5902-888e-df2fb5a3bd0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513828} {:answer/id #uuid "84feaf94-72bf-5421-abe7-2cb440d49da6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513878} {:answer/id #uuid "8e5dea63-94f7-5b8d-8a9d-2375d5e03ec5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513900} {:answer/id #uuid "aed08239-7725-54b6-a37b-ad604cc72dec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513990}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24a04d7d-0766-53f9-bf1a-56af16878e80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "◻" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513634} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c41e6d8-d02a-5d03-aa80-6b777df73834" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514280}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bf7a3bf9-7841-5c39-8953-649f06640b22" :question/math-academy-id "q-181262" :question/problem "Which of the following is an element of the set $A=\\{♢,\\,10,\\,a,\\,◻\\}?$" :question/worked-solution "The elements of our set are as follows:\n\n$$\n♢,\\,10,\\,a,\\,◻\n$$\n\nAmong the given options, the only element that belongs to the set is $◻.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514475 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054849 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "de59db4d-82d5-5bad-a559-bf5396375355" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Non-Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0127109a-3730-548f-bf3d-07a26a3905f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{1,f,2,g\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513529} {:answer/id #uuid "5bb2439b-f439-585e-abab-de3ea1a458a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{∅,\\{f,g\\}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513777} {:answer/id #uuid "e1204290-3544-5af4-bfb1-86ea28a53325" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{f,\\{h\\}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514122} {:answer/id #uuid "f47e1594-3e4e-52fc-b3b4-036ed29b53bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514170} {:answer/id #uuid "ff43a729-f5c5-5a8e-a699-84816fa6c4a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f,g,h" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514207}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff43a729-f5c5-5a8e-a699-84816fa6c4a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f,g,h" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514207} :answer-field/id #uuid "841027ba-dd4e-5448-93c3-df146c3ec885" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514290}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f2f32264-6492-5e60-8c09-298d7626357d" :question/math-academy-id "q-80275" :question/problem "Which of the following is **not** a set?" :question/worked-solution "A set is a collection of elements listed between two braces (curly brackets). However, note that the null set (the set that does not contain any elements) can be written as either $\\{\\}$ or $∅.$\n\n- $f,g,h$ is *not* a set. The letters $f,$ $g,$ and $h$ are *not* listed between two braces.\n\nAll the other choices are sets.\n\n- $\\{f,\\{h\\}\\}$ is a set. The elements are $f,$ and $\\{h\\},$ and they are listed between the two outermost braces.\n\n- $\\{∅,\\{f,g\\}\\}$ is a set. The elements are $∅,$ and $\\{f,g\\},$ and are listed between the two outermost braces.\n\n- $\\{\\}$ is a set. It is the null set.\n\n- $\\{1,f,2,g\\}$ is a set. The elements are $1,$ $f,$ $2,$ and $g,$ and they are listed between two braces."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514474 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054850 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "900f0d3d-6a5c-53b2-b987-eee1a8963b6b" :knowledge-point/title "Using Element Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15fd2bc1-c68a-55a5-bd2a-a662816264a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0\\in Y$ and $\\pi ,\\sqrt{2}\\notin Y$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513589} {:answer/id #uuid "a7a22407-4ed6-5a83-8beb-894b416066bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1,\\pi ,\\sqrt{2}\\notin Y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513966} {:answer/id #uuid "c6fdb368-49f9-53cd-8d4a-966db82c4693" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0,1,\\pi ,\\text{e}\\in Y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514053} {:answer/id #uuid "f202e225-7c13-544d-919d-7cf5555f73f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\pi ,\\text{e},\\sqrt{2}\\in Y$ and $0,1\\notin Y$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514162} {:answer/id #uuid "fc797368-1b18-5f08-84b5-498afafdbc38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\pi ,\\text{e},\\sqrt{2}\\notin Y$ and $0,1\\in Y$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514192}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f202e225-7c13-544d-919d-7cf5555f73f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\pi ,\\text{e},\\sqrt{2}\\in Y$ and $0,1\\notin Y$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514162} :answer-field/id #uuid "54aa798f-1fb7-558c-8c8b-32e0cf00221c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514263}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f10fdf14-c3b0-5ff7-a1e1-67a02a7a3852" :question/math-academy-id "q-80286" :question/problem "If $\\pi ,\\text{e}$ and $\\sqrt{2}$ are elements of $Y$, but $0$ and $1$ are not, then which of the following is true?" :question/worked-solution "If $a$ is an element of $S,$ we write $a\\in S.$ Otherwise, if $a$ is *not* an element of $S,$ we write $a\\notin S.$\n\n- Since $\\pi ,\\text{e}$ and $\\sqrt{2}$ are elements of $Y,$ we write $\\pi ,\\text{e},\\sqrt{2}\\in Y.$\n\n- Since $0$ and $1$ are *not* elements of $Y,$ we write $0,1\\notin Y.$\n\nAll together, we have the following statement:\n\n$\\,$  $\\pi ,\\text{e},\\sqrt{2}\\in Y$ and $0,1\\notin Y$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514367 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054851 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ceb6c84-a16b-5519-abd6-d2bb72ea81d3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Set Corresponding to a Description"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06d8ffd2-50f9-5666-8b0a-9d861689836a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{…,13,14,15\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513547} {:answer/id #uuid "0f39c390-6ae8-57ba-a0c8-09fbb39812dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{1,3,5,…,14\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513568} {:answer/id #uuid "141ad6e6-6929-578e-bacc-9597f6a3ef43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{1,2,3,…,15\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513583} {:answer/id #uuid "976b9ccb-f7eb-5fd8-aab8-ccbbc0ace82c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{1,2,3,…,14\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513923} {:answer/id #uuid "b21b2b22-ae8e-5dff-acd6-97c845f86570" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{…,12,13,14\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513997}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "141ad6e6-6929-578e-bacc-9597f6a3ef43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{1,2,3,…,15\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513583} :answer-field/id #uuid "42187262-f8cb-5e17-9c88-a9b4b6fc1094" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514254}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "101cf0dd-9e7d-5358-b3ec-977545014b49" :question/math-academy-id "q-80294" :question/problem "Which set represents all positive integers less than or equal to $15?$" :question/worked-solution "To express the desired set, we start with the first positive integer less than or equal to $15,$ which is $1.$ The next positive integer is $2,$ the one after that is $3,$ and so on up to $15$ (which is the last number that is less than or equal to $15$).\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n\\{1,2,3,…,15\\}.\n$$"}]}
